        "original_id": "b329e3a7-ba6c-54b2-bb5b-4a37a571d773",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Mountbatten Institute\n- People: Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma; Patricia, 2nd Countess Mountbatten; Prince Philip, Duke of Edinburgh; Elizabeth II\n- Roles: British naval officer; statesman; Admiral of the Fleet\n\nFacts:\n- Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma, was born as Prince Louis of Battenberg on 25 June 1900.\n- Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma, was a British naval officer, a statesman, and held the rank of Admiral of the Fleet.\n- Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma, was an uncle of Prince Philip, Duke of Edinburgh, and a second cousin once removed of Elizabeth II.\n- Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma, died on 27 August 1979.\n- Mountbatten Institute was founded in 1984.\n- Mountbatten Institute was named in honour of Louis Mountbatten, 1st Earl Mountbatten of Burma.\n- Mountbatten Institute was benefacted by Patricia, 2nd Countess Mountbatten, who was Louis Mountbatten's eldest daughter.",
